The deploy failed because `Decimal.compareTo` doesn't exist in Apex, so the class didn't compile and the trigger couldn't see it. I replaced those calls with plain `==` comparisons. I haven't re-run the deploy or tests after this change. I also made two small hardening changes:

- The new pipeline total is rounded to the Currency field's decimal scale, so the "only update if changed" check can't see a false difference.
- The class runs `without sharing`, so the totals are computed over all opportunities no matter who runs the DML, as a native roll-up would.

